Release 1.6.0 (August 2026)
---------------------------
* Detect TAP-Windows adapters whose packet reader fails during startup and
  automatically retry with the bundled Wintun backend
* Prevent concurrent processes using one secure identity from repeatedly
  evicting each other's live session; the active owner keeps its sticky IP and
  an inactive owner can be replaced after a bounded ownership timeout
* Classify duplicate/replayed secure packets separately from authentication
  failures and rate-limit genuine authentication warnings
* Fix the exact 32-packet ACK bitmap gap boundary without an undefined shift
* Add protocol v5, which pre-authenticates every Noise handshake message with
  a randomized XChaCha20-Poly1305 envelope and encrypts the established
  message type and complete adaptive-transport header; the wire retains only
  the per-session receiver index and replay counter needed for demultiplexing
  and AEAD nonce construction, with no fixed Hans magic value
* Make clients try v5 first while retaining automatic v4/v3/v2/v1 fallback;
  allow servers to use `--require-v4` to reject unencrypted v1-v3, and add
  `--require-v5` for clients that refuse downgrade and servers that silently
  ignore every earlier protocol before allocating handshake state
* Make a pinned server fingerprint implicitly refuse unencrypted v1-v3
  fallback, so compatibility negotiation cannot discard the pin
* Extend protocol, wrong-key, tamper, replay, package-isolation, userspace,
  IPv6, direct-mode, bidirectional TCP, and server-restart recovery tests to v5

Release 1.5.1 (August 2026)
---------------------------
* Restore encrypted data-plane performance with in-place AEAD, contiguous ACK
  tracking, optimized release builds, and single-threaded opportunistic Linux
  packet batching
* Raise the userspace TCP send and receive windows for high-bandwidth,
  higher-latency VPN paths to 6 MiB and 8 MiB respectively instead of capping
  throughput at one small window per round trip
* Improve userspace TCP loss recovery with a finer lwIP timer while retaining
  a conservative 400 ms retransmission floor for jittery Internet paths
* Add opt-in all-TCP-port userspace sharing with explicit mappings taking
  precedence, and harden listener failure and bridge teardown paths
* Use conventional sequential ICMP echo tokens for current sessions, add
  per-peer gap/late/duplicate telemetry, and briefly reorder only inner data
  after a late packet proves the path reorders; loss-only and normal paths
  remain zero-copy and do not incur reorder delay
* Fairly service IPv4 and IPv6 ICMP when unrelated echo traffic keeps one raw
  socket busy, and securely follow authenticated ICMPv6 replies sourced from
  another address on a multi-address server
* Recover encrypted v4 clients after a server restart or expired server-side
  session using authenticated ICMP heartbeats and a jittered client-initiated
  handshake; unknown receiver indexes remain silent and expose no reset oracle
* Expand sanitizer, mixed userspace concurrency, lossy SOCKS UDP, portability,
  package-isolation, and real transport recovery coverage

Release 1.5.0 (August 2026)
---------------------------
* Add encrypted protocol v4 with Noise XXpsk3, Argon2id, X25519,
  ChaCha20-Poly1305, receiver indexes, and replay protection
* Bind sticky peer identity to the authenticated Noise public key
* Add server-key pinning, optional downgrade refusal, and identity inspection
* Add RFC 1929 SOCKS5 authentication with a private password file
* Add JSON peer listing and portable ICMP/entropy diagnostics
* Add complete v4 framing, tamper, wrong-PSK, replay, and package tests
* Add IPv6 server-name/literal resolution and ICMPv6 as an outer carrier;
  the virtual VPN network remains IPv4
* Switch authenticated peer traffic inside the server without host iptables,
  and use LocalAppData for native Windows state
* Restrict Linux kernel echo suppression to active peers and protect native
  Windows identity keys with owner-only ACLs before writing them

Release 1.4.0 (July 2026)
-------------------------
* Add an optional adapter-free userspace client using statically embedded lwIP
* Add SOCKS5 TCP CONNECT and UDP ASSOCIATE access to every VPN peer
* Add inbound VPN port sharing with loopback-by-default and explicit target maps
* Add unprivileged ping-socket support on POSIX systems and Windows IP Helper transport
* Add isolated-package userspace integration tests without TUN or build dependencies

Release 1.3.0 (July 2026)
-------------------------
* Add protocol v3 with session-scoped sequence numbers and rolling ACKs
* Replace the default fixed poll window with adaptive request credits
* Probe and use direct echo replies, with automatic fallback and re-upgrade
* Add transport unit tests and privileged failure/recovery CI coverage

Release 1.2.0 (July 2026)
-------------------------
* Add persistent random client device identities
* Add server-side sticky leases with least-recently-seen offline eviction
* Add peer listing, device-id inspection, and protocol fallback for old servers
* Add Wintun and Linux veth adapter fallbacks with safe orphan cleanup and
  veth offload handling
* Publish stripped, isolated-package builds across Linux, BSD, macOS, and
  Windows, including static musl and legacy Windows i386 packages

Release 1.1.0 (November 2022)
-----------------------------
* Switch to utun devices on macOS (thanks to unkernet)

Release 1.0.0 (November 2016)
-----------------------------
* Added cygwin support
* Remove supplementary groups when dropping privileges
* Fixed compile error on FreeBSD

